Original commit body from 7bb3a45e2a823f2d81bc5d5538e2ed2ebc602991:

Addresses INV-fogum. ADR-0049 ruling 2 clause 3's shadow reached only the
boundary arm. One verify-claims run over a Go handler writing to a
request-chosen path printed `no-net-recv` as confirmed_with_caveats
[deferred_crossing] and `untrusted-input-no-host-fs` as a bare `confirmed`.

A clean taint verdict now carries a `deferred_crossing` caveat (arm "taint")
for each shadowed boundary B with AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP[B] equal to the
claim's source label. net_recv and db_read both derive untrusted_input, so
_merge_caveat now keeps deferred-crossing caveats per boundary and re-renders
the sentence when a fold widens the site list. host_secret and
host_description claims are untouched; a violated verdict never acquires it.

Measured on the item's repro (production CLI): untrusted-input-* claims go
confirmed -> confirmed_with_caveats; host-secret-* stay confirmed. On
gocryptfs 501d5a5 no verdict value moves; the two untrusted_input verdicts
gain the caveat.

ADR-0049 and measurement 0010 credited gocryptfs's `inconclusive` to this
shadow. Re-run on dev, that verdict carries no deferred_crossing caveat; it
is the coverage gate (54 launch sites, 61 unclassified modules). Both
documents are corrected, and the net_recv registry description no longer
says the shadow "blocks" a verdict "and nothing else".

